## FIBONACCI_CLI_MAIN
- [IMPL-FIBONACCI_CLI] [ARCH-FIBONACCI_CLI_SCRIPT] [REQ-FIBONACCI_PRINT] How: Parse one COUNT token, generate the sequence, print one integer per stdout line.
Contract:
  INPUT: ARGV (list of string)
  OUTPUT: stdout lines; process exit status
  CONTROL: ARGV
  PRE: none (validates internally)
  POST: when exit 0, stdout has count lines matching GENERATE_FIBONACCI_SEQUENCE(count) as one integer per line; when exit 1, no sequence on stdout
  EFFECTS: IO
  FAILURE_MODES: MISSING_ARG; EXTRA_ARG; INVALID_ARG
  TERMINATION: total
  unit-testable: composition (entry-point binding)

procedure FIBONACCI_CLI_MAIN:
  # [IMPL-FIBONACCI_CLI] [ARCH-FIBONACCI_CLI_SCRIPT] [REQ-FIBONACCI_PRINT] How: Parse one COUNT token, generate the sequence, print one integer per stdout line.
  1. WRITE DEBUG argc to stderr
  2. IF length(ARGV) == 0:
       WRITE "Usage: ruby scripts/fibonacci.rb COUNT" to stderr
       EXIT 1
  3. IF length(ARGV) > 1:
       WRITE "Usage: ruby scripts/fibonacci.rb COUNT" to stderr
       EXIT 1
  4. SET token = ARGV[0]
  5. IF token does not match unsigned decimal digits:
       WRITE "error: COUNT must be a non-negative integer" to stderr
       EXIT 1
  6. SET count = integer value of token
  7. WRITE DEBUG count to stderr
  8. SET sequence = RUN IMPL-FIBONACCI_GENERATE_SEQUENCE GENERATE_FIBONACCI_SEQUENCE(count)
  9. WRITE DEBUG length(sequence) to stderr
  10. FOR each n IN sequence:
        WRITE n and a newline to stdout
  11. EXIT 0
